 "_note": "Read from the page images of the scanned volume, not from its OCR: the OCR of these pages loses minus signs and reads reference codes as numbers (an earlier automatic extraction gave Ni a coefficient of 7383). Values the volume prints in parentheses are its own mark for an estimate and are listed under 'uncertain'; a '?' in the volume is omitted here. Where the volume gives several determinations the first firm one is taken, and its range is recorded. lb29_tempcoef.py reproduces the same rows automatically and is kept as a cross-check, not as the source. Scandium has no coefficient in either table. Thallium appears in both: the hexagonal row is the one that matches the library's record.",
